<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Socialist Republic of the Union of Burma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1974–1988</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Socialist Republic of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> was the official name of Burma under the one-party constitution of 1974. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ne-win">Ne Win</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma-socialist-programme-party">Burma Socialist Programme Party</a> the state followed the 'Burmese Way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialism">Socialism</a>', with nationalised industry and isolation from the outside world. It ended with the uprising of 1988 and the military takeover that followed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/socialist-republic-of-the-union-of-burma.jpg" alt="Socialist Republic of the Union of Burma" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Myanmar_(1974%E2%80%932010).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
